id: pm-vcs-kr28
title: Converge the pm toolchain on 2026.9.5 and match git merge recency
description: "Pin @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.5, pm-changelog ^2026.9.2, and pm-ops 2026.9.5. Preview called mergeItemDocuments with the SDK default (ours-wins) while the git driver uses latest_document_update, so a conflicted scalar was predicted as ours=1 while git merge retained the later updated_at. Point preview at the driver's recency policy and assert the real merge against that primitive, not a pinned branch-direction winner. Acceptance scripts and README now use pm package install."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-05T18:24:14.141Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-05T18:24:44.202Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-05T18:24:44.186Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-05T18:24:44.186Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
resolution: "Preview now calls mergeItemDocuments with conflictResolution=latest_document_update, matching runMergeDriver. The behavioral test compares the working-tree priority to that primitive and requires the fixture to distinguish recency from ours-wins."
expected_result: "release:check and pm health --strict-exit both exit 0 on the pinned toolchain."
actual_result: "Coverage 758/758 at 100%. Revert-proof of preview predicts exactly what a real merge produces: 1 fail against the ours-wins assertion (3 !== 1), 1 pass after the recency property."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-05T18:24:36.441Z",pi-agent,"Pinned @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.5, pm-changelog ^2026.9.2, pm-ops 2026.9.5. The git item merge driver now uses conflictResolution=latest_document_update; preview still called mergeItemDocuments with the SDK default preferred_side, so the suite asserted ours-wins priority 1 while git merge retained the later updated_at (priority 3). Preview now passes the driver override. The test asserts the real merge matches the driver primitive and that this fixture actually distinguishes recency from ours-wins. Revert-proof: old assertion failed 1/0 (3 !== 1), restored test passed 1/0. Acceptance scripts and README use pm package install because install is the deprecated alias."
